  "effect_is_inside_the_frozen_topology_control_policy": true,
  "fairness_note": "Mission staging is owner decision 1 and is gated purely by a robot's own frozen lifecycle state, so any policy that opens an intent stages identically -- S2 does, for its one forced attempt. The asymmetry is that the online policy opens intents repeatedly and the fixed baselines by construction do not. That is a property of the policies, not of the evaluation, so it is not a fairness defect; it is nonetheless the reason this cell may not be counted as completed-reconfiguration headroom.",
  "family": "F5",
